# Trivy Ignore File
# These CVEs affect OS packages in python:3.13-slim (Debian) with no upstream fix.
# Reviewed: 2026-05-19. Re-review by: 2026-08-31.

# ncurses buffer overflow — not used by application code (terminal library)
CVE-2025-69720

# systemd arbitrary code execution — not the init system inside containers
CVE-2026-29111

# nghttp2 DoS — base image residual; not used by application code
CVE-2026-27135

# glibc iconv() DoS — fix deferred by Debian; app does not use iconv with untrusted character sets
CVE-2026-4046

# curl / libcurl4t64 — SMB connection reuse and cookie leak; app uses HTTPS only, not SMB
# Reviewed: 2026-05-19. Re-review by: 2026-08-31.
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276

# libgnutls30t64 — all DTLS-specific vulnerabilities (zero-length fragment DoS, NUL-char auth bypass,
# heap overflow, nameConstraints bypass, packet reordering DoS, name constraint bypass);
# app makes TCP/HTTPS calls only with no DTLS exposure. No Debian fix available.
# Reviewed: 2026-05-19. Re-review by: 2026-08-31.
CVE-2026-33845
CVE-2026-42010
CVE-2026-33846
CVE-2026-3833
CVE-2026-42009
CVE-2026-42011

# libssh2 integer overflow via large username/password — app does not use SSH in any container
# Reviewed: 2026-05-19. Re-review by: 2026-08-31.
CVE-2026-7598

# libkrb5 / Kerberos DoS via integer underflow (libgssapi-krb5-2, libk5crypto3, libkrb5-3, libkrb5support0)
# No Debian fix available. App does not use Kerberos or GSSAPI; these packages are
# transitive OS-level dependencies of the python:3.13-slim base image.
# Reviewed: 2026-05-21. Re-review by: 2026-08-31.
CVE-2026-40356

# perl-base — Archive::Tar symlink/hardlink path traversal, IO::Compress arbitrary code execution,
# Perl heap buffer overflow, and memory exhaustion via crafted archives.
# No Debian fix available. App is a Python-only data ingestion pipeline (JSON fetch → pandas → GCS).
# perl-base is a transitive OS-level dependency of python:3.13-slim; Perl is never invoked at runtime.
# Reviewed: 2026-06-03. Re-review by: 2026-09-30.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538

# libsqlite3-0 — SQLite <3.53.2 memory-corruption / heap overflow. No Debian fix
# available; transitive OS dep of python:3.13-slim. App uses DuckDB in-memory, not
# system libsqlite3 against untrusted SQL.
# Reviewed: 2026-06-23. Re-review by: 2026-09-30.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# cryptography GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf — bundled OpenSSL in cryptography wheels. Fix is
# 48.0.1, but cryptography 48.x crashes ("Illegal instruction") at runtime on arm64
# (Raspberry Pi 5 dashboard host); pin held at 46.0.5 in pyproject.toml. Low exposure:
# used only by google-auth for GCS token signing over HTTPS, no untrusted TLS input.
# Reviewed: 2026-06-23. Re-review by: 2026-09-30.
GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Debian 13.6 base-image CVEs with no upstream fix (Status: affected, Fixed
# Version: none). Reviewed against fuel-dashboard: a FastAPI app that reads
# Parquet from GCS over HTTPS and queries DuckDB in memory.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-10. Re-review by: 2026-11-10.

# curl / libcurl4t64 — SSH host verification bypass via schemeless SFTP/SCP URLs
# (12064), insecure connection establishment on TLS config mismatch (8286),
# unauthorized connection reuse (8458), and information disclosure via uncleared
# proxy credentials (8927).
# curl IS invoked here: spain_fuel_api.fetch shells out to it (realtime_client).
# Exposure is bounded by how it is called — one hardcoded https:// constant
# (DATA_SOURCE_URL), TLS pinned with --tlsv1.2/--tls-max 1.2, no proxy flags, no
# credentials, and a one-shot subprocess per fetch so no connection pool is
# reused across hosts. No user-supplied URL ever reaches curl.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8458
CVE-2026-8927

# perl-base — regex engine returning silently incorrect results (13221,
# CRITICAL), information disclosure via integer overflow in pack/unpack (57432),
# and Storable signed integer overflow (57433). Perl is a transitive dependency
# of python:3.13-slim and is never invoked; the app is Python-only.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433

# gzip — global buffer overflow in the LZH decoder. The app never shells out to
# gzip and never handles .lzh archives; Parquet is read via pyarrow (snappy).
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 — symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl functions. The
# container runs a single non-interactive app process and performs no ACL
# operations on attacker-controlled paths.
CVE-2026-54369

# util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, util-linux) — integer
# overflow in libblkid DOS partition parsing. The app never inspects block
# devices or partition tables; libblkid is a base-image transitive dep.
CVE-2026-53615

# cryptography 46.0.5 — CVE-2026-69247 (fix 50.0.0) and CVE-2026-69249 (fix
# 49.0.0). Held at 46.0.5 by constraint-dependencies in the root pyproject.toml
# because 48.x+ crashes ("Illegal instruction") on arm64, the Raspberry Pi 5 the
# dashboard runs on. Used only by google-auth to sign GCS tokens over HTTPS — no
# untrusted key or certificate input. Bumping needs an arm64 container test
# first; tracked separately from this suppression.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-10. Re-review by: 2026-11-10.
CVE-2026-69247
CVE-2026-69249
